  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Krypkille. Logic: Misere trick-taking with special deck. Key: Harlekin dual value, Hus blocks exchanges, avoid penalty cards.',
    Player: "Krypkille is a Swedish misere game with a unique 42-card deck. Two of each card exist. Harlekin is highest when led, lowest when second. Avoid winning tricks. Use Hus to block exchanges. Don't get stuck with Kuku or Katt!",
    objective: "Score as few points as possible by avoiding capturing tricks or holding 'lowest' cards.",
    gameplay: "1. Standard trick-taking. Must follow suit (if suits are used) or rank.\n2. In Krypkille, the player with the *HIGHEST* card wins the trick (and thus 'penalty' cards).\n3. **The Harlekin**: Changes value. If led, it is the highest. If played later, it is the lowest.",
    keyRules: [
      'Two of each card in the 42-card deck',
      'Harlekin is highest when led, lowest when played second',
      "Hus (Home) blocks exchanges - 'Home stays'",
      'Kuku (Cuckoo) penalty when received',
      'Avoid winning tricks to avoid penalty points',
    ],
